# L §5.16: "An ask line's own projection is no decision: it reads an amount after t by its random clause, by the
# line's query, or on a path by that path's sample (§5.14.1)". The reality of L5_16_projection_random with no
# clause: on path 1 the projection reads the samples, here every address of spend pinned to 900.00 PLN (L §5.16 Pins
# `with sample growth[*] = e`): 10 000 - 3 * 900 = 7 300.00 PLN (r5); the line's query over the paths is the same
# on both paths, standard error 0 (r6).
=== m.tally
model r
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source own "own"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind spends: event certain
  leg cash: PLN
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2020-01-01..
place shop: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input spend_mu: money PLN
input spend_sd: money PLN
input spend_dom: int
def spend[m in months]: dist PLN = normal(spend_mu, spend_sd) to 1e-9 at end_of(m)

move buy[m in months]: spends
  on day_of(m, spend_dom)
  at end_of(m)
  leg cash from konto to shop amount round(spend[m], minor(PLN), half-even)

version v
  cite own
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-01-01
  spend_mu = 1 000.00 PLN "own"
  spend_sd = 100.00 PLN "own"
  spend_dom = 15 "own"
  opening[konto] = 10 000.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "statement"

ask r5: bal(konto, 2026-03-31) from 2026-01-01 with sample spend[*] = 900.00 PLN paths 2 seed 1 path 1
ask r6: mean(bal(konto, 2026-03-31) from 2026-01-01) with sample spend[*] = 900.00 PLN paths 2 seed 1
=== expect
r5: 7 300.00 PLN
  pinned sample: spend[*] = 900.00 PLN
  held: spend_dom = 15 (v), read for 2026-02-01
  held: spend_dom = 15 (v), read for 2026-03-01
  held: spend_dom = 15 (v), read for 2026-04-01
  cut 2026-01-01
r6: 7 300 PLN (standard error 0; 2 paths; horizon 2026-04-01)
  pinned sample: spend[*] = 900.00 PLN
  held: spend_dom = 15 (v), read for 2026-02-01
  held: spend_dom = 15 (v), read for 2026-03-01
  held: spend_dom = 15 (v), read for 2026-04-01
  cut 2026-01-01
